#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0311 expect=violation domain=CO
#note "THE ABSENT-TARGET ARM of is_(not_)unique_set (EC-53 / Fix #143). No COSEQ column at all: the absent target is DROPPED from the key tuple and the check regroups on the surviving key [USUBJID], so rows 1 and 2 both fire and row 3 is unique. This rule carries NO var_exists guard on COSEQ, unlike its sibling CDISC-SEND-0312 which authors one on POOLID, which is exactly why it moves. Do NOT pin COSEQ -- the column does not exist. ESCALATE if this reports 0 or SKIPPED."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 2
#expectViolationAt row=1 USUBJID=001
#expectViolationAt row=2 USUBJID=001
dataset CO
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col COVAL   type=Char label="Comment"
---
S1 | CO | 001 | First
S1 | CO | 001 | Second
S1 | CO | 002 | Third
---
